---
description: Automatic khabro-* subagent routing and the mandatory fresh-reviewer quality shield for apps/, packages/ and infra/ changes
alwaysApply: true
---

The coordinating agent routes work to the [khabro-* subagents](../../.claude/agents/khabro-principal-engineer.md)
on its own; the user should never have to name one. Skip routing only for questions,
docs-only edits and changes under ~10 lines.

| When the task… | Run, in order |
| --- | --- |
| is a new feature, spans API + client, or is ambiguous | `khabro-principal-engineer` (plan) → `khabro-design-director` (art direction, if it has a screen) → `khabro-ux-engineer` (spec, if user-facing) → implementers in parallel on disjoint files → reviewers |
| touches `apps/api` code | `khabro-backend-engineer` |
| adds or changes an EF migration, `infra/migrations`, an index or a hot query | `khabro-database-engineer` |
| touches `apps/app` (Expo reader) logic: navigation, hooks, data fetching | `khabro-mobile-engineer` |
| touches `apps/admin`, `apps/site`, reader styling, tokens or screen polish | `khabro-frontend-engineer` (loads `ui-taste`, `ios-design`, `apple-design`; brand in `docs/brand.md`) |
| touches motion, transitions, gestures or haptics | `khabro-motion-engineer`; screens consume its primitives |
| changes OpenAPI or `packages/shared-types` | `khabro-backend-engineer` + `pnpm generate:types`; `khabro-architecture-reviewer` reviews |
| touches CI, `render.yaml`, Cloudflare Pages, `infra/docker` or ingest workflows | `khabro-platform-engineer` |
| fixes a bug or lacks coverage | `khabro-test-engineer` (failing test first) |
| needs a GitHub issue, progress comment, commit/PR into `qa` or promotion | `khabro-git-steward` |
| deploys, changes env vars, promotes `qa` → `main`, or hits a failed deploy, health check or ingest run | `khabro-ops-watcher` (diagnose; redeploy only when told); `khabro-sre` for incidents and reliability work |
| finishes a substantial task (after reviewers pass) | `khabro-skill-curator` (capture new or repeated procedures as skills); the coordinator inspects its diff |

Each subagent file lists its required skills; the coordinator passes the task condition in
the brief. The coordinator itself uses `khabro-feature-delivery`,
`subagent-driven-development`, `using-git-worktrees`, `incremental-implementation`, and
`debugging-and-error-recovery` when a gate fails (all in `.agents/skills`).

After any non-trivial implementation, spawn fresh reviewers in parallel; the author may
not approve their own diff:

- always `khabro-code-reviewer`;
- `khabro-security-reviewer` for admin auth, CORS, rate limits, secrets, untrusted feed
  content, public endpoints, CI or deploy config;
- `khabro-performance-reviewer` for queries, migrations, ingestion, caching or feed lists;
- `khabro-architecture-reviewer` for dependencies, contracts, module boundaries or schema
  direction;
- `khabro-ux-engineer` and `khabro-design-director` for user-facing screens or UI
  primitives; a design dimension under 8 is a Required finding.

Rules:

- If a named subagent type is unavailable, spawn a general-purpose subagent told to follow
  the matching `.claude/agents/khabro-*.md`; put the agent name in the task description so
  the review gate hook recognizes reviewers.
- Give reviewers the task, diff, source and acceptance criteria — not the author's
  conclusion. Do not rubber-stamp.
- Do not push or promote with Critical or Required findings open.
- Multi-agent work uses disjoint files; the coordinator integrates.
- The [review gate hook](../hooks/review-gate.mjs) sends the agent back to run
  the matching reviewers when gated code changed since the last review. Answer it; do not
  disable it.
- `pnpm` checks and `ci.yml` are the mechanical gate; fresh reviewers are the agent gate.
